{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>You led in Your lovingkindness this people that You redeemed.</b> From the time You redeemed them — when You brought them out beyond the border of Egypt and they came to Succoth — You began to guide them on the way, as it says: וַיִּסְעוּ מִסֻּכֹּת וַה' הֹלֵךְ לִפְנֵיהֶם (Exodus 13:20–21)." "<b>You guided them by Your strength.</b> You guided them gently on dry ground within the sea, as it says: מוֹלִיכָם בַּתְּהֹמוֹת כַּסּוּס בַּמִּדְבָּר לֹא יִכָּשֵׁלוּ (Isaiah 63:13)." "<b>To Your holy habitation.</b> By a straight path to journey toward Your holy habitation, in order to sanctify them there for Your service."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:41.975964575Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}